<h3 id="section-3">Section 3: Investigators</h3>
<p>At minimum, a Corresponding Investigator is required for submission. Mark any additional investigators as Contributing (Figure 8).</p>

<h4>Corresponding Investigator</h4>
<p>The corresponding author(s) on the published (or to-be-published) manuscript associated with this study, and the primary contact for questions about the data. The corresponding investigator reviews the study and submits it to ROSSA. If your study has multiple corresponding authors, please include information for all of them.</p>

<h4>Contributing Investigator</h4>
<p>Anyone else on the study. Select Contributing on its own. It cannot be combined with Corresponding, and it is not required for submission.</p>

<h4>Adding yourself</h4>
<p>If you are an investigator on the study, click <strong>Add myself</strong> to fill in the form from your ROSSA account. If no corresponding investigator has been added yet, Corresponding is selected for you. Review the details, adjust the role if needed, and add any information that is missing.</p>

<figure>
    <img src="{{ asset('images/guides/data-ingestion/08_Investigator.png')}}" alt="Investigators interface" class="img-fluid mb-3 border">
    <figcaption class="text-muted"><strong>Figure 8. Adding Investigator Information.</strong> Step 1: Optionally click “Add myself” to fill in your details. Step 2: Select Corresponding, or select Contributing on its own. Step 3: Fill out the investigator’s information. Step 4: Click the “Add Investigator” button. Repeat as necessary.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h4>Investigators and collaborators</h4>
<p>Investigators are credited on the public study record. People who only help you fill out the submission, such as a lab member or core facility staff, do not need to be listed as investigators. To invite them, click the <strong>Share</strong> button at the top right of the page. Everyone you share the study with can edit it, but only a corresponding investigator can submit it. A collaborator who has finished their part can use <strong>Send for approval</strong> on the Submission page to ask the corresponding investigator to review and submit the study.</p>
